  "title": "iPhone Duo Launches with Face Unlock Feature, Limited Security",
  "summary": "Apple introduces a limited face unlock feature for the iPhone Duo, along with Touch ID, while the phone features a nano-texture finish and a 7.6-inch inner display. Analysts assess if this design could impact security and pricing.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Apple's iPhone Duo features a 5.4-inch outer display and a 7.6-inch inner display, with a 'nano-texture' finish and a Touch ID on the power button.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The iPhone Duo now borrows a feature from the new HomeView, allowing it to recognize mugshots, but the security is limited compared to Face ID.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apple's iOS 27.3 beta includes a face unlock feature that uses the front-facing camera for authentication, though it's not as secure as Face ID.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
